---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Structure from '../components/Structure.astro';
import InterfaceMap from '../components/InterfaceMap.astro';
import ActionDemo from '../components/ActionDemo.astro';
import { specification } from '../data/specification';
import '../styles/home.css';
---

<Base title="Email agents can act on">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero container">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>
          Email agents
          <br />
          can <span>act on.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-description">
          Services already ask people to make decisions by email. Mail Action Protocol describes
          those requests so an agent or inbox can understand them, check the current proposal and
          help you act.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-buttons">
          <a class="button primary" href="/specification">
            Read the specification <Icon size={17} />
          </a>
          <a class="hero-secondary" href="#decision-example">
            Follow a decision <span>↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <a href="/specification" class="protocol-kicker">
          <span class="small-dot"></span>
          <span>Mail Action Protocol · {specification.status}</span>
          <Icon size={13} />
        </a>
      </div>
      <Structure />
    </section>
    <section
      class="decision-section container"
      id="decision-example"
      aria-labelledby="decision-heading"
    >
      <div class="section-intro">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-line">From message to action</span>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="decision-heading">
            There’s work
            <br />
            in your inbox.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          A campaign is ready to send. Review the email and audience, then decide. Your inbox checks
          the current request with the service.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ActionDemo />
    </section>
    <section class="map-feature container" aria-labelledby="map-title">
      <div class="map-feature-mark">
        <span class="eyebrow">The specification</span>
        <div class="big-map">
          MAP<span>↗</span>
        </div>
        <div class="map-feature-meta">
          <span>MAIL ACTION PROTOCOL</span>
          <span class="pill">{specification.status}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="map-feature-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">Mail Action Protocol</span>
        <h2 id="map-title">Describe it once.</h2>
        <p>
          A type gives a decision the same meaning across services. Campaign approval names what
          will be sent, by whom, to which audience and when. Each service keeps its own interface
          and permissions.
        </p>
        <p>
          MAP defines what the email says and what must be checked before anyone acts. A connection
          you approved uses the service's existing operations.
        </p>
        <a href="/specification" class="button dark-button">
          Read MAP <Icon size={17} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="demo-section container" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-line">The service keeps its interface</span>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="demo-heading">
            An email.
            <br />
            Your existing service.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            A request arrives by email. MAP says what the decision means. The service can keep its
            existing API, tool or messaging system, provided it can check permission and the exact
            proposal when the decision is made.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/interfaces">
            Explore the interface research <Icon size={16} />
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <InterfaceMap />
    </section>
    <section class="ecosystem container" aria-labelledby="ecosystem-heading">
      <div class="ecosystem-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-line">MailSchema Types</span>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="ecosystem-heading">
          A type gives the request its meaning.
        </h2>
        <p class="ecosystem-description">
          Sending a campaign, publishing an article, confirming an address and reporting unfamiliar
          account activity are different decisions. Each type says exactly what its choices mean.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ecosystem-links">
        <a class="ecosystem-types" href="/specification/contracts">
          <div class="ecosystem-link-top">
            <Icon name="layers" size={33} />
            <Icon name="northeast" size={24} />
          </div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Read the rules</span>
          <h3>Type contracts</h3>
          <p>See how a type defines an action's choices, exact terms and outcomes under MAP.</p>
          <span class="text-link">
            How types work <Icon size={17} />
          </span>
        </a>
        <a class="ecosystem-registry" href="/registry">
          <div class="ecosystem-link-top">
            <Icon name="grid" size={33} />
            <Icon name="northeast" size={24} />
          </div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Find a definition</span>
          <h3>Registry</h3>
          <p>
            Browse shared definitions for real decisions, inspect examples, and see whether a
            service supports them.
          </p>
          <span class="text-link">
            Browse type definitions <Icon size={17} />
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="open-section container">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-line">Contribute</span>
        <h2>
          Propose a type
          <br />
          <span>for your workflow.</span>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          If your service asks people to decide something by email, show the request and what each
          choice does. A useful type should work for more than one service.
        </p>
        <a href="/contribute" class="button outline">
          Prepare a type proposal <Icon size={17} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
